    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5381" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμόθεν</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμόθεν</span></b> , Adv.:
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμός</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>from some place or other,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἀμόθεν γε, θεά, . . εἰπὲ καὶ
					ἡμῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.10
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁ. γέ ποθεν</span>”
				<i>from some quarter or other,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					492d
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lg.</u>
				798b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ.</span> alone, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				1.401
			</span></i>.</div>
